n.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:319:### 7.3.4 References to code inside a continuation\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:393:## §7.4 Safepoints — where a canonical configuration exists (blocker 1)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:395:### 7.4.1 Only safepoints lift, and the table is the machine's\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:488:### 7.4.2 Safepoint maps for foreign engines: static facts only\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:545:### 7.4.3 The pending wait travels as data — complete, and resumable elsewhere\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:696:## §7.5 Recursive portable encoding (blocker 2)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:698:### 7.5.1 A disjoint tagged grammar\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:822:### 7.5.2 Primitives: a name is a binding, not a meaning\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:885:### 7.5.3 Sharing, cells, and cycles\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:967:### 7.5.4 Failure is total and names its place\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:992:## §7.6 Dependency closure and context (blocker 3)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:994:### 7.6.1 Declared, not hand-written — and discovered conservatively\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1069:### 7.6.2 The store slice, restored as an isolated store\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1140:### 7.6.3 The migration unit is one task\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1172:### 7.6.4 Modules\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1185:### 7.6.5 The satisfaction check\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1213:## §7.7 Ownership arbitration — custody as a lease over datoms (blocker 4)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1215:### 7.7.1 The race, named\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1230:#